# What a run leaves behind. results/raw.tsv is the exception -- it is the
# battery's accumulated output and is checked in, so it is unignored below.
# results/* rather than results/, because the tool does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation for a file inside one never takes effect
# and adding results/raw.tsv is refused.
results/*
!results/raw.tsv
kubeconfigs/
# Per-run scratch: the subnet counter that survives create/delete cycles, the
# kind config written only when KUBELET_V asks for one, and the pinned pid of
# Docker Desktop's VM.
.machine-subnet-seq
.kind-config.yaml
.docker-vm-pid
# Previous raw.tsv files, kept when a run replaces them. Useful locally for
# comparing against an earlier machine or an earlier ferry; not history the
# repository needs to carry.
results-archive/
# The Deployment manifests run.sh renders per replica count.
.dep-*.yaml
